{:adr-id "2607220000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-4329 — Other Construction Installation Operations-Coordination Actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :context
 "ISIC 4329 (Other construction installation -- thermal/acoustic
  insulation, sound-proofing, elevator/escalator installation, other
  specialty building installation work not elsewhere classified,
  distinct from 4321 electrical / 4322 plumbing-heat-cool installation)
  had a :spec-only placeholder pointing at a never-created
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-F4329 repo (gh api 404 confirmed at the real
  cloud-itonami org before any work began; live registry :name verified
  to match the assigned premise exactly). Lower physical-risk trade
  domain than the demolition/road-rail siblings this fleet's robotics-
  premise actors mirror structurally -- no heavy equipment near public
  traffic, no structural-collapse risk from the actor's own coordinated
  work; relevant hazards are attic/roof/elevator-shaft fall risk and
  legacy materials hazards (asbestos-containing insulation) disturbed by
  retrofit work."
 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4329 mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4330
  (Building Completion and Finishing) module-for-module: Installation
  Advisor ⊣ Installation Governor + audit ledger. Eight HARD gates:
  unknown op, effect-not-propose, forbidden action class (trade-
  equipment-control/direct-actuation/installation-completion-sign-off),
  site-not-verified, legal-basis-missing, hazmat-survey-incomplete,
  fall-protection-noncompliant, unresolved-safety-concern. MemStore/
  DatomicStore backends, fully portable .cljc with NO JVM interop
  anywhere in src/ (installation.notify uses a caller-injected function
  transport seam instead of embedding java.net.http). No new Rust code,
  no robot-control code -- coordination-only, :itonami.blueprint/robotics
  false. Like 4330 and unlike 4311/4210: :schedule-installation-operation
  is NOT a permanent high-stakes member -- MAY auto-commit at phase 3
  when clean+confident, reflecting building-installation trade work's
  materially lower risk profile than demolition/heavy-civil earthwork
  scheduling. Per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/DEU) pre-work hazmat-survey +
  fall-protection legal-basis catalog, every citation independently
  verified (WebFetch against osha.gov for the new USA asbestos citation;
  JPN/DEU citations reused verbatim from finishing.facts, both being
  generic cross-trade OSH regulations) before being written. USA hazmat
  citation deliberately DIFFERS from finishing.facts's EPA lead-paint
  surface-coating rule -- cites 29 CFR 1926.1101 (OSHA asbestos
  construction standard) instead, the domain-appropriate legal basis for
  legacy asbestos-containing insulation (vermiculite attic fill, pipe/
  duct lagging) disturbed during installation/retrofit work."
 :consequences
 ["Certified building-installation operators fork and deploy independently with auditable coordination records; trade-equipment control and installation-completion sign-off remain permanent, un-overridable HARD blocks"
  "Second coordination-only actor in this fleet (after 4330) whose own schedule op is deliberately lower-stakes than its structural siblings' -- reinforces the pattern as reusable for future trade-craft (vs heavy-civil) construction verticals"
  "USA hazmat-survey legal-basis choice (OSHA asbestos standard vs. finishing's EPA lead-paint rule) establishes a precedent: pick the domain-appropriate hazmat citation for the actual materials/work at risk rather than defaulting to whatever a structurally similar sibling actor already cites"
  "kotoba-lang/industry registry entry \"4329\" promoted :spec -> :implemented, :repo/:business-id corrected from the stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-F4329 placeholder to cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4329, :required-technologies narrowed to drop :robotics/:dmn/:bpmn/:cae (this actor has no CAE/robotics/BPMN dependency)"]
